⚠ HP-0 IS THE ROW TO COPY. Without it HP-5's zero is indistinguishable from
agreement, and the two mean opposite things. The counter is built out of the
refusal arm's own semantics rather than out of a return value: htSet sets htFlag
to 0, calls setParse, then sets htFlag to 1 -- and a refusal STOPS THE BLOCK, so
the second assignment never runs. A take is a flag that reached 1.

